  "interpretation": [
    "Four failed rate cases describe two distinct left-foot reverse-playback windows: the Walk trajectory is the same geometry at 2, 4 and 6.5 m/s. Every failure remains a failure under the declared baseline+2 mm maximum drift gate.",
    "The persistent points travel a shorter total horizontal path, yet their maximum and net distance from the window start increase. Net movement can cancel, so neither lower path length nor improved p95 overrides the maximum-drift failures.",
    "At the final maximum drift the selected points are 21.22 mm (Walk) and 29.10 mm (Run) above the floor, while another part of the same foot remains below20 mm. Their complete height ranges are about10.26–33.14 mm and8.96–32.60 mm. This is compatible with rolling a foot rather than holding a flat sole, but does not prove that the added drift looks natural.",
    "The source intentionally lowers the animated pelvis by4 cm to provide knee flexion; in these near-seam windows pelvis differences reach41.08/43.19 mm and chest differences41.17/42.26 mm. Actor root transforms, rig rest geometry and physics heights are not shifted. Upper LOCAL track preservation does not mean unchanged upper WORLD position.",
    "The candidate removes the observed earlier iteration knee angular spike and reduces broad slip and loop velocity seams. Finite-difference knee acceleration remains higher than baseline in places; there is no zero-slip, biomechanical, physical-device or Fortnite-level quality claim.",
    "Release may use the separately recorded actual-controller and moving-scene reviews to judge this bounded tradeoff. This independent script does not certify all proposed improvement gates, and no gate was reduced to fit the candidate."
  ],
